WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.980
<b>Faculty Office</b>

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:10.620
Nice to meet you.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.290
I've been asked to coach the rugby team.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.760
My name is Komori.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.490
Oh, hello.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.640
I'm Yoshida, the team's adviser.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.460
A practice game?

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:35.470
I see. You want to test the results
of the training camp.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:40.410
I don't mind if that's what 
you and the team want to do.

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:43.440
But is there anyone who will play you?

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.790
For some reason, Keijo is always 
inviting us to play against them,

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.030
but they're the exception.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:59.640
And the other schools don't have 
time for Jinko's ball games.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:04.430
I haven't tried speaking to them directly,
so I can't say for sure, though.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.940
So long as no one gets hurt
or causes any disciplinary issues,

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:11.500
you're free to do whatever.

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:17.500
Was there something else?

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:23.040
Have you seen them play?

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:23.770
What?

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:26.890
A while ago, I guess.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:32.650
Did it look to you like they 
were playing "ball games"?

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.970
What? Oh.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:40.550
They may have begun to take things 
seriously since you joined the team,

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:43.660
but what I saw was, well...

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:48.170
Have you seen their club room?

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:49.670
No.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:54.670
They had a mountain of 
tatty old rugby textbooks.

00:01:56.050 --> 00:02:00.180
It's hard to imagine a time when 
they weren't taking it seriously.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:08.190
Yoshida-san, you've neglected
your duty as educator.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.590
H-How dare you!

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:13.400
I'm doing what I have to do as their adviser!

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.340
Besides, I respect their independence...

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:17.450
That's not what I meant.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:25.450
It's your responsibility 
to say: "Ready. Set. Go."

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:30.670
You show them where the start line is,
 which way they have to run,

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.250
and then, you send them off 
with a "Ready. Set. Go."

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:41.220
The sky's the limit for children
if you do that for them.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.100
Without an adult doing that for them,

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:50.790
they'll complete three years of high school
without even finding that start line,

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:52.980
much less sprinting toward their goals.

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:59.050
Ignoring them doesn't 
foster their independence.

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:08.160
Are you done?

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:09.790
Forgive me.

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:15.650
The team being ignored made me feel so bad,
I couldn't help but lecture you.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:19.730
There were only two things 
I wanted to discuss.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:24.210
First, I want you to let me handle them.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:28.000
And second...

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.470
<b>Todo-dai Sagami</b>

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:11.450
<b>practice game</b>

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.460
We're playing Todo-dai Sagami in a practice game.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:19.250
<b>Episode 8   Ball Games</b>

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:17.270
Todo-dai Sagami?

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:22.720
Isn't Sagami supposed to 
be a school full of geniuses?

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:25.010
They have a rugby team, too?

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:31.510
Gion-kun, Sagami came second in
 last year's prefectural preliminaries.

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:34.890
Sekizan.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:40.250
An acquaintance of mine
just happens to coach their team.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:43.530
Apparently, they're willing to
come to our field.

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:47.080
Have you played Sagami before?

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:48.530
No.

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:52.800
I see. It'll be a good
learning experience, then.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:58.040
And I told your adviser 
to come watch the game.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.140
Pull yourselves together.

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.550
Let's get practice started.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:09.050
Y-Yes, sir!

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.610
The second-placed team, huh?

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:18.340
I've been itching to find out if our 
training camp has changed anything...

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:20.060
Let's go.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:22.940
Practice like your lives depend on it.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:26.190
All right! Let's win this time.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:31.040
You should be worrying about whether or not 
you'll even be playing, you little turd.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:32.030
What was that?!

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.790
You didn't even play in the Keijo game,
you no-good thug!

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:35.650
What?!

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:38.830
Okay, okay. No fighting.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:53.220
I'm responsible for saying "Ready. Set. Go"?

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:59.310
Where's a simple ball game going to get them?

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:08.240
Boy, I'm so nervous. Sagami's scary.

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:12.200
Yoshida-sensei hasn't turned up.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:15.990
He probably doesn't care about our game.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:19.380
Sagami should be arriving shortly.

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:22.120
Make sure you're warmed up.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.670
So this is Jinko, huh?

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.760
That was a long trip.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:36.870
H-Hey, you'd better not mess up
in front of Jinko's coach.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:39.240
You're more likely to mess up than we are.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:43.020
There he is.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:45.520
Hey, Komori-san!

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.720
Long time, no see!

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:53.600
Look at that guy.
He used to play for the national team!

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:55.700
Yeah, we know.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:59.000
Komori-san, it's Kita! Kita!

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.320
I know.

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:03.080
He was my junior.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:09.300
Sorry for making you come here
when you placed second.

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:12.160
It's totally fine.

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:12.970
Excuse me.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.050
Who's your captain?

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:16.650
Oh, right...

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:20.950
Uh, Wada-san, Jinko's looking for you.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.810
I'm Wada, the captain.

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:28.600
I'm Sekizan, Jinko's captain.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:32.010
I've heard of you.

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:34.960
That's one crazy hairstyle you've got.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:35.700
Thanks for coming.

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:44.070
<i>Why is he so intense?</i>

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:49.450
Sorry. Our captain's
a bit intimidating, isn't he?

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:52.480
Uh, yeah, just a little.

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:54.880
Will you be playing in the game?

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:55.710
Yeah.

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:57.590
I see. Good luck to both of us.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:01.030
He made the starting lineup as a first-year.

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:02.640
Really? That's amazing.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:05.080
Hey, don't do that!

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:08.300
Our first-years might play, too.

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:09.820
Thanks in advance for playing us.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:19.430
No, thank you. The pleasure's all ours.

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:21.380
Talk to you later.

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:22.400
Sure.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:29.140
There's an annoying guy on their team.

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:31.460
Let's kill them.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.410
Uh, sure...

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:37.730
Our club room is over there. 
You can leave your bags in it.

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:39.670
Sure, thanks.

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:41.640
Come on! Let's go!

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:43.080
Run!

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:44.140
Yes, sir!

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:54.000
Top schools are different 
from the rest of us.

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:57.420
But I'm sure we're just as determined to win.

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:00.500
Let's fight with everything we've got.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.280
Let's have a good game!

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:13.420
You guys sure are inseparable.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:13.800
<b>Bench</b>

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:14.300
<b>Bench</b>

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:14.800
<b>Bench</b>

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:15.420
<b>Bench</b>

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:18.180
I know Jinko's #10.

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.680
He's a first-year.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:22.430
Seriously? Can we play like we always do?

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:23.900
Sure.

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:27.700
They've got some reasonably big forwards.

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:41.820
There's not a single girl cheering for us.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:43.740
How sad.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:51.750
I've got it.

00:11:05.210 --> 00:11:06.990
Iwashimizu, are you okay?

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:08.500
Ouch...

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:09.560
I'm fine.

00:11:17.930 --> 00:11:19.510
They're gunning for him.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:25.580
Jinko's #5 is just big. Go for him.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:29.750
That's Zuma Middle School's Iwashimizu.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:31.650
Have you played against him before?

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:37.500
In middle school, I lost to him 
in the prefectural semifinals.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:43.010
Oh, well... In that case, 
we'd better crush them.

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:47.030
I want to talk 
to Komori-san

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:47.030
Komori-san is 
still so cool

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:47.030
Komori-san, 
Komori-san

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:47.030
Fidget 
Fidget

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:47.030
Glance
 Glance

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:47.030
Fidget 
Fidget

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:50.020
Komori-san is 
still so cool

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:50.020
Komori-san,
Komori-san

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:50.020
Fidget
Fidget

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:50.020
Glance
Glance

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:50.020
Glance
Glance

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:50.020
Coach, 
please 
focus on
 the game

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:50.020
Also, 
you're 
being 
creepy

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:53.130
Over here!

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:05.910
Iwashimizu!

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.160
Get the ball moving!

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:19.110
Sorry, Mr. Giant. I didn't mean to do that.

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:26.930
Hey! You did that on purpose!

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:28.490
What are you guys doing?

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:31.130
Kashima-senpai, the bleeding's stopped.

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:33.370
I'm fine. Let's go.

00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:50.150
Knock-on by Jinko.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:54.160
S-Sorry.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:09.450
Here comes the high punt!

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:18.190
Mark!

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:22.610
"Mark"?

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.100
What does "mark" mean?

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:25.730
Quit asking me questions!

00:13:25.730 --> 00:13:27.360
Go ask Ume!

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:28.200
Ow!

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:34.890
If you catch a ball kicked by your 
opponent inside your 22 meter line...

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:39.250
while saying "mark," you get a free kick.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:40.950
Why?

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:45.200
I don't know. I guess it's your 
reward for making a clean catch.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:49.760
<b>"The Nice 
Catch Award"</b>

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:46.360
Why would they do that?

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:49.760
In any case, you can't tackle 
someone if they've marked the ball.

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:56.860
Wow, you got it all the way here?

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:58.980
You can kick the ball pretty far.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:04.390
You can have it back!

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:09.400
Jeez. Can't you try running a little, #10?

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:10.780
Mark—

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:16.750
But he marked it.

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:21.290
Oh, sorry. Are you okay?

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:25.930
Sagami #13, be careful.

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:27.670
Okay.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:30.930
Isn't tackling against the rules?

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:31.990
Yeah. Yeah.

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:35.220
He couldn't stop himself and ran into him.

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:36.180
Yeah. Yeah.

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:38.690
Tsk. Ow...

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:40.960
Sorry, Oharano-kun.

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:48.580
I know who you are.

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:53.580
You've been really good since rugby school.

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:58.290
Has your bratty little brother 
gotten any better at the game?

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:05.710
Oh, right. Sorry, I forgot.

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:10.470
Your brother quit playing because of you.

00:15:13.780 --> 00:15:16.140
Oh, sorry.
That has nothing to do with the game.

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:17.130
Forget I said anything.

00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:33.070
Hey, let go!

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:33.820
Let go!

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:35.830
Hey, ref! Are you blind?

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:37.580
He just grabbed my jersey!

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:45.290
If you've got time to complain 
to the ref, go after the ball!

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:47.170
Huh? What did you say?!

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.670
Stop, Hirokuni!

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:51.590
Try saying that again, first-year!

00:15:59.150 --> 00:16:02.440
Quit fighting, bro.

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:10.330
Do things seem a little strange to you?

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:21.710
You disgust me, Zuma Middle School punk.

00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:27.930
How long are you going to keep playing rugby?

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:33.970
You probably don't remember,

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:39.970
but I lost to you guys in the prefectural 
semifinals when we were in middle school.

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:42.350
Well, I say "you guys,"

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:46.360
but really, it was just your captain.

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:50.360
Miyuki, right?

00:16:50.830 --> 00:16:55.860
That creep who walked over to us
 with a grin on his face after the match.

00:16:56.270 --> 00:16:59.960
He got hurt in training right 
after that semifinal, didn't he?

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:03.750
He wasn't in the final.

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:11.090
And you got destroyed in the final.

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:15.770
Why couldn't you have hurt him sooner?

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:20.720
If it wasn't for him,
we would've made it to Nationals.

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:40.930
Iwashimizu, calm down.

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:42.120
Okay?

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:51.650
I-I'm sorry.

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:55.630
Huh...

00:18:00.110 --> 00:18:01.760
Oh no, you don't!

00:18:14.370 --> 00:18:16.030
Jinko, over the top.

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:21.280
What are you doing, Iwashimizu-kun?!

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:38.930
It's Sagami's line-out.

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:44.880
We've got the maul!

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:47.210
Push!

00:18:59.350 --> 00:19:01.160
The goal line's right behind us!

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:04.200
Push harder, Iwashimizu!

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:24.820
Try!

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:47.620
They've been completely overwhelmed.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:50.370
Don't you think their play 
is a little rough?

00:19:57.450 --> 00:20:02.760
It is. They're walking a fine line out there.

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:06.350
They're verbally provoking our players, too.

00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:10.010
But it's all a gray area.

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:13.600
As a strategy, it's more valid than not.

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:24.520
Their barely-legal plays are making our 
players too angry to make the right calls.

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:27.710
The game's moving at Sagami's pace.

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:34.870
The way Kita's taught them to play
is not very nice at all.

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:40.380
Dammit.

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:47.890
How can I play like this?

00:20:57.020 --> 00:21:00.710
Oh, dear. It went out of bounds.

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:03.250
Nice kick!

00:21:14.890 --> 00:21:19.000
Oh, come on! What the <i>hell</i> is going on?! God!

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:22.630
I messed up because the team's 
body language is the pits!

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:25.260
I've had enough of all of you!

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:26.330
You're starting to piss me—

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:27.270
Oharano.

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:33.710
You're out.

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:39.980
Now there's a surprise... not!

00:21:43.870 --> 00:21:45.360
Kill yourselves.

00:22:01.770 --> 00:22:05.130
I told you so.

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:07.090
In the end...

00:22:10.270 --> 00:22:12.820
they're only messing around in a ball game.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
<b>Next Time: "You've Gotten Stronger"</b>

00:23:45.770 --> 00:23:49.190
Next time: "You've Gotten Stronger."
